|~ qlang operand catalog — typeClassifier family. `:type` is the
   canonical identity-tag reader: it returns the value's TagKeyword
   (for tagged-instance Maps, error values, conduits, snapshots) or
   its plain Keyword (for scalars and base containers). Asking
   what a value is means composing that reader with `eq` —
   `| type | eq(:string)` — so the family holds one operand.
   A Map declaring `:kind ::Foo` answers `::Foo`, the identity it
   declares, rather than `:map`. ~|

:type
  |~~ Returns the value's identity tag. For tagged values
      (errors, conduits, snapshots, tagged-instances, builtin
      descriptors) returns the TagKeyword stamped on the
      value's JS-header `TAG_HEADER_SYMBOL` slot. For scalars
      and base containers returns the plain Keyword that names
      the kind (`:number`, `:string`, `:keyword`, `:vec`,
      `:map`, `:set`, …).

      `result !| type` is the user-facing path to an error's
      tag identity — the materialised descriptor exposed by
      `!|` is a Map with the per-site `::ErrorTag` riding on
      the JS-header slot, and `type` reads through the same
      invariant every other tagged value-class shares.

      ~{42 | type | eq(:number)}
      ~{"hi" | type | eq(:string)}
      ~{:foo | type | eq(:keyword)}
      ~{[1 2] | type | eq(:vec)}
      ~{::conduit[[] ~{42}] | type | eq(::conduit)}
      ~{
        "hello" | add(1)
        !| [type /actualType]
        |  eq([::AddLeftNotNumberError :string])
       }
  ~~|
  ::builtin{:impl :qlang/prim/type
            :category :typeClassifier
            :subject :any
            :returns :keyword
   }
